IMPORT prelude

-- Interactive Gambling Act 2001 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- which online gambling may lawfully be offered to me, what
-- a wagering app may take from me, and how I can exclude myself through the National Self-exclusion Register (BetStop).
--
-- SEAT: the gambler -- the individual in Australia who bets, plays or buys tickets online -- "Which online gambling is
-- lawful to offer me? Am I committing an offence by using it? May the app give me credit or take my credit card? Can I put
-- myself on the Register, for how long, and can I come off it? Can my family put me on it? Once I am on it, what must the
-- betting companies do?". Every exported question is that person's. The Act's offences and civil penalties are all laid on
-- providers ("A person commits an offence if ... the person intentionally provides ..."); none is laid on the customer, and
-- the encoding says so (s 15, 15AA, 15C, Part 7B). Where the Act hands a judgment to someone else (the Minister's or the
-- regulations' conditions for an exclusion; the Register operator's identification procedure; "as soon as practicable"),
-- it is asked as a fact and the answer is conditional on it.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 4 (gambling service, wagering service, illegal interactive gambling service, unlicensed regulated
-- interactive gambling service); s 5 (prohibited interactive gambling service) with s 8 (Australian-customer link), s 8AA
-- (telephone betting service), s 8A (excluded wagering service), s 8B (excluded gaming service), s 8BA (place-based betting
-- service), s 8BB (trade promotion gambling service), s 8D (excluded lottery service), s 8E (regulated interactive gambling
-- service), s 10B (in-play betting service); ss 15, 15AA (who commits the offence); s 15C(1), (1A), (3), (3A), (4A) and s 15D
-- (as one input) (credit and credit cards); s 69A (as what it permits); Part 7B: s 61GB (licensed interactive wagering
-- service), ss 61JA, 61JB, 61JC (registration), 61JD (inducements), 61JF, 61JG (duration and extension), 61JH(2), (3) (warning
-- before expiry), 61JK (removal on my application), 61JM, 61JN(5) (removal on other grounds), 61KA (no wagering services to
-- me), 61LA-61LD (no marketing to me), 61MA (no new account), 61MB, 61MC (closing my existing account and paying me out).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 24, compilation date 14 October 2024, includes amendments to Act No. 38, 2024 (register id
-- C2024C00646), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00851.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026).
-- NOT DEPOSITED: the Interactive Gambling (National Self-exclusion Register) Rules 2022 (the Register rules: the manner of
-- applying, the identification procedure, the period within which the operator must register me, the listed support
-- services), the Minister's determinations of conditions under ss 8AA(2), 8A(2), (4), (6), 8B(2), 8BA(2), 8BB(2) and 15C(4A)(d),
-- and the regulations under ss 8C, 8D(1A) and 69A. Every number or condition they set is an INPUT here: whether the conditions
-- for an exclusion are met; whether my identity has been verified or need not be; whether a support service is listed.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: designated broadcasting and datacasting links (s 8C), financial products (s 5(3)(b)), wholesale services
-- (s 5(3)(ba)), exempt services (s 10); the provider's ignorance defences (ss 15(3), 15AA(5), 15C(5), (5A)) and the due
-- diligence defences in Part 7B (they excuse the provider, they do not make the service lawful to offer me); Part 2A
-- (designated countries); s 15E; the complaints system beyond who may complain (Parts 3-6); the advertising prohibition
-- (Part 7A); the Register's information rules, levy and review (Part 7B Divisions 7-9 and ss 61JI, 61JJ, 61JL beyond their
-- effect on me); penalties in penalty units. Casinos, poker machines in venues and lotteries bought over the counter are
-- State law; Crown Perth's self-exclusion program is the casino's own.
--
-- PERIODS are whole months and days counted by the caller ("months since my registration came into force", "days since I
-- applied", the day of application being day 0). This is the encoder's convention, not the Act's.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Interactive Gambling Act 2001 -- from the seat of the gambler`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a whole number` IF `n` EQUALS TRUNC `n` 0

§§ `ss 4, 5, 8-8E, 10B -- what kind of service it is`

-- s 4: "gambling service means: (a) a service for the placing, making, receiving or acceptance of bets; or (b) a service the
-- sole or dominant purpose of which is to introduce individuals who wish to make or place bets to individuals who are willing
-- to receive or accept those bets; or (c) a service for the conduct of a lottery; or (d) a service for the supply of lottery
-- tickets; or (e) a service for the conduct of a game, where: (i) the game is played for money or anything else of value; and
-- (ii) the game is a game of chance or of mixed chance and skill; and (iii) a customer of the service gives or agrees to give
-- consideration to play or enter the game". "wagering service means a service covered by paragraph (a) or (b)".
-- s 10B: "an in-play betting service to the extent to which: (a) the service relates to betting on the outcome of a sporting
-- event, where the bets are placed ... after the beginning of the event; or (b) ... on a contingency that may or may not happen
-- in the course of a sporting event ... after the beginning of the event."
DECLARE `Kind of gambling` IS ONE OF
    `betting on a horse, harness or greyhound race`
    `betting on a sporting event, placed before it begins`
    `betting on a sporting event, placed after it begins`
    `betting on another event or contingency, such as an election`
    `betting on the outcome of a lottery`
    `a lottery or lottery tickets, not an instant lottery`
    `an electronic scratch or other instant lottery`
    `a game of chance or of mixed chance and skill, such as online pokies, casino games or poker`

-- One gambling service, as the gambler meets it. The facts are ones the customer can see or be told.
DECLARE `Gambling service` HAS
    `what it offers` IS A `Kind of gambling`
    `is provided in the course of carrying on a business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is provided over the internet, a phone or other carriage service, or by broadcasting or datacasting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all my dealings with it are by live voice call` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is provided on equipment at a venue for anyone there to use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is run in connection with a competition to promote trade` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider holds a State or Territory licence for that kind of service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `any conditions set by the Minister or the regulations for its exclusion are met` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a wagering service` IF
    CONSIDER `the service`'s `what it offers`
    WHEN `a lottery or lottery tickets, not an instant lottery` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an electronic scratch or other instant lottery` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a game of chance or of mixed chance and skill, such as online pokies, casino games or poker` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 5(1): "a prohibited interactive gambling service is a gambling service, where: (a) the service is provided in the course
-- of carrying on a business; and (b) the service is provided to customers using any of the following: (i) an internet
-- carriage service; (ii) any other listed carriage service; (iii) a broadcasting service; (iv) any other content service;
-- (v) a datacasting service." s 8E(1)(i), (j) repeat the same two limbs.
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is provided interactively` IF
        `the service`'s `is provided in the course of carrying on a business`
    AND `the service`'s `is provided over the internet, a phone or other carriage service, or by broadcasting or datacasting`

-- s 8AA(1): "a telephone betting service is a gambling service, where: (a) the service is provided on the basis that dealings
-- with customers are wholly by way of voice calls made using a carriage service; and (aa) the service does not relate to
-- betting on the outcome of a lottery; ... and (b) the conditions (if any) determined under subsection (2) have been
-- satisfied." (8): not one if a bet, bet type, amount or confirmation "can be provided by a customer otherwise than by way of
-- a voice call". s 8AA(3), (4): a voice call is a live spoken conversation, not a recorded or synthetic voice or tones.
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a telephone betting service` IF
        `the service`'s `all my dealings with it are by live voice call`
    AND (NOT (`the service`'s `what it offers` EQUALS `betting on the outcome of a lottery`))
    AND `the service`'s `any conditions set by the Minister or the regulations for its exclusion are met`

-- s 8A(1): excluded "to the extent to which the service relates to betting on ... (a) a horse race; (b) a harness race; (c) a
-- greyhound race". (3): "(a) ... betting on ... sporting events; and (b) ... not an in-play betting service". (5): "(a) ...
-- betting on ... an event ... or a contingency; that is not covered by subsection (1) or (3); and (b) ... not an in-play
-- betting service; and (c) ... not ... (i) a service for the conduct of a scratch lottery or other instant lottery; ...
-- (iii) a service relating to betting on the outcome of a lottery; ... (iv) a service for the conduct of a game covered by
-- paragraph (e) ...". Each "so long as the other conditions (if any) determined ... have been satisfied".
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an excluded wagering service` IF
    `the service`'s `any conditions set by the Minister or the regulations for its exclusion are met`
    AND CONSIDER `the service`'s `what it offers`
        WHEN `betting on a horse, harness or greyhound race` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `betting on a sporting event, placed before it begins` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `betting on another event or contingency, such as an election` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 8B(1): "an excluded gaming service is a service for the conduct of a game covered by paragraph (e) ... (a) ... provided to
-- customers who are at a particular place; and (b) ... dealings with customers involve the use of electronic equipment made
-- available to customers at that place; and ... available for use by any customer who is at that place; so long as: (c) the
-- provider of the service holds a licence ... that authorises the provision of the service at that place".
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an excluded gaming service` IF
        `the service`'s `what it offers` EQUALS `a game of chance or of mixed chance and skill, such as online pokies, casino games or poker`
    AND `the service`'s `is provided on equipment at a venue for anyone there to use`
    AND `the service`'s `the provider holds a State or Territory licence for that kind of service`
    AND `the service`'s `any conditions set by the Minister or the regulations for its exclusion are met`

-- s 8BA(1): the same, for "a service covered by paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition of gambling service" (betting).
-- Simplification: s 8BA(1)(b)(iii) (the equipment is not shared with another provider's service) is taken as met.
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a place-based betting service` IF
        `is a wagering service` `the service`
    AND `the service`'s `is provided on equipment at a venue for anyone there to use`
    AND `the service`'s `the provider holds a State or Territory licence for that kind of service`
    AND `the service`'s `any conditions set by the Minister or the regulations for its exclusion are met`

-- s 8D(1): "an excluded lottery service is: (a) a service for the conduct of a lottery; or (b) a service for the supply of
-- lottery tickets." (1A): subject to conditions in the regulations (for example, not "a highly repetitive or frequently drawn
-- form of a keno-type lottery"). (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply to an electronic form of: (a) scratch lottery; or (b)
-- other instant lottery."
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an excluded lottery service` IF
        `the service`'s `what it offers` EQUALS `a lottery or lottery tickets, not an instant lottery`
    AND `the service`'s `any conditions set by the Minister or the regulations for its exclusion are met`

-- s 8BB(1): "a trade promotion gambling service is: (a) a service for the conduct of a lottery, where the lottery is conducted
-- in connection with a competition for the promotion of trade; or (b) a service for the conduct of a game of chance or of
-- mixed chance and skill, where the game is conducted in connection with a competition for the promotion of trade".
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a trade promotion gambling service` IF
        `the service`'s `is run in connection with a competition to promote trade`
    AND (NOT (`is a wagering service` `the service`))
    AND `the service`'s `any conditions set by the Minister or the regulations for its exclusion are met`

-- s 5(3): "none of the following services is a prohibited interactive gambling service: (a) a telephone betting service;
-- (aa) an excluded wagering service ...; (ab) an excluded gaming service ...; (aba) a place-based betting service ...; ...
-- (ae) an excluded lottery service ...; ... (bb) a trade promotion gambling service".
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls in an exclusion that is regulated` IF
       `is a telephone betting service` `the service`
    OR `is an excluded wagering service` `the service`
    OR `is an excluded gaming service` `the service`
    OR `is a place-based betting service` `the service`
    OR `is an excluded lottery service` `the service`

@export Is this a prohibited interactive gambling service, one that may not be offered to anyone in Australia (s 5)?
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service` @desc The gambling service: what it offers, how it reaches you, and whether the provider is licensed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a prohibited interactive gambling service` IF
        `is provided interactively` `the service`
    AND (NOT (`falls in an exclusion that is regulated` `the service`))
    AND (NOT (`is a trade promotion gambling service` `the service`))

-- s 8E(1): a regulated interactive gambling service is one of the excluded kinds (telephone betting, excluded wagering,
-- excluded gaming, place-based betting, excluded lottery, ...) provided interactively. (4): not "(b) a trade promotion
-- gambling service".
@export Is this a regulated interactive gambling service, lawful only with a State or Territory licence (s 8E)?
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service` @desc The gambling service: what it offers, how it reaches you, and whether the provider is licensed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a regulated interactive gambling service` IF
        `is provided interactively` `the service`
    AND `falls in an exclusion that is regulated` `the service`
    AND (NOT (`is a trade promotion gambling service` `the service`))

§§ `ss 8, 15, 15AA -- may it be offered to me`

-- s 8: "a gambling service has an Australian-customer link if, and only if, any or all of the customers of the service are
-- physically present in Australia."
-- s 15(2A): "A person must not provide a prohibited interactive gambling service that has an Australian-customer link".
-- s 15AA(3): "A person must not provide a particular kind of regulated interactive gambling service if: (a) the service has
-- an Australian-customer link ...; and (b) the person does not hold a licence (however described) under a law of a State or
-- Territory that authorises the provision of that kind of service". (7): a licence in one State covers providing it "(b)
-- outside the State or Territory" too.
DECLARE `Lawfulness` IS ONE OF
    `outside the Act, because it is not provided as a business over the internet, a phone, broadcasting or datacasting`
    `outside the Act's prohibitions, because it is a trade promotion gambling service`
    `outside the Act's prohibitions while I am outside Australia`
    `prohibited: no one may provide it to me while I am in Australia`
    `lawful to provide to me: a regulated service whose provider holds a State or Territory licence for it`
    `unlawful to provide to me: a regulated service whose provider holds no State or Territory licence for it`

@export Is it lawful to provide this gambling service to me (ss 5, 8, 15, 15AA)?
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service` @desc The gambling service: what it offers, how it reaches you, and whether the provider is licensed
      `I am physically present in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are physically in Australia when you use it
GIVETH A `Lawfulness`
DECIDE `Is it lawful to provide this service to me` IS
    IF NOT `is provided interactively` `the service`
    THEN `outside the Act, because it is not provided as a business over the internet, a phone, broadcasting or datacasting`
    ELSE IF `is a trade promotion gambling service` `the service`
         THEN `outside the Act's prohibitions, because it is a trade promotion gambling service`
         ELSE IF NOT `I am physically present in Australia`
              THEN `outside the Act's prohibitions while I am outside Australia`
              ELSE IF `Is it a prohibited interactive gambling service` `the service`
                   THEN `prohibited: no one may provide it to me while I am in Australia`
                   ELSE IF `the service`'s `the provider holds a State or Territory licence for that kind of service`
                        THEN `lawful to provide to me: a regulated service whose provider holds a State or Territory licence for it`
                        ELSE `unlawful to provide to me: a regulated service whose provider holds no State or Territory licence for it`

-- ss 15(1), 15AA(1): "A person commits an offence if: (a) the person intentionally provides" the service. Penalty: 5,000
-- penalty units, each day a separate offence; civil penalty 7,500 penalty units (ss 15(2A), 15AA(3)). No provision of the
-- Act makes it an offence or a contravention to be the customer.
DECLARE `Who is liable` IS ONE OF
    `no one under this Act, because providing it to me is not prohibited`
    `the provider, not me: the Act's offences and civil penalties fall on whoever provides the service`

@export If this service is provided to me unlawfully, who commits the offence: me or the provider (ss 15, 15AA)?
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service` @desc The gambling service you use
      `I am physically present in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are physically in Australia when you use it
GIVETH A `Who is liable`
DECIDE `Who commits the offence if this service is provided to me` IS
    CONSIDER `Is it lawful to provide this service to me` `the service` `I am physically present in Australia`
    WHEN `prohibited: no one may provide it to me while I am in Australia`
        THEN `the provider, not me: the Act's offences and civil penalties fall on whoever provides the service`
    WHEN `unlawful to provide to me: a regulated service whose provider holds no State or Territory licence for it`
        THEN `the provider, not me: the Act's offences and civil penalties fall on whoever provides the service`
    OTHERWISE `no one under this Act, because providing it to me is not prohibited`

@export Do I commit an offence under this Act by gambling with this service?
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service` @desc The gambling service you use
      `I am physically present in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are physically in Australia when you use it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence by gambling with it` IF
    -- Every offence in the Act is the provider's (or an ISP's, or an advertiser's); none is the customer's. The facts are
    -- asked only so the question can be put about a particular service; the answer does not turn on them.
    FALSE

-- s 4: "illegal interactive gambling service means a prohibited interactive gambling service that is provided in
-- contravention of subsection 15(2A)." s 69A(1): "The regulations may provide: (a) that an agreement has no effect to the
-- extent to which it provides for the payment of money for the supply of an illegal interactive gambling service; and (b)
-- that civil proceedings do not lie against a person to recover money alleged to have been won from, or paid in connection
-- with, an illegal interactive gambling service." The regulations are not deposited.
DECLARE `Winnings answer` IS ONE OF
    `s 69A does not reach it, because it is not an illegal interactive gambling service`
    `it is an illegal interactive gambling service: regulations under s 69A may void the agreement and bar suing for money won from it, and they are not deposited`

@export Could I be unable to sue for money won from, or paid to, this service (s 69A)?
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service` @desc The gambling service you used
      `I am physically present in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were physically in Australia when you used it
GIVETH A `Winnings answer`
DECIDE `Could I be unable to recover money from this service` IS
    IF `Is it lawful to provide this service to me` `the service` `I am physically present in Australia`
        EQUALS `prohibited: no one may provide it to me while I am in Australia`
    THEN `it is an illegal interactive gambling service: regulations under s 69A may void the agreement and bar suing for money won from it, and they are not deposited`
    ELSE `s 69A does not reach it, because it is not an illegal interactive gambling service`

§§ `ss 15C, 15D -- credit, credit cards and digital currency`

-- s 15C(3): "A person who provides a regulated interactive gambling service that is a wagering service must not: (a) provide,
-- or offer to provide, credit in connection with the service to a customer ... who is physically present in Australia; or (b)
-- facilitate or promote the provision of credit, by a third person". (3A): nor "accept, or offer to accept, payment in
-- connection with the service using a method mentioned in subsection (4A)". (4A): "(a) a credit card; (b) an account, service
-- or facility in which payment is made from a credit card linked to the account, service or facility; (c) digital currency;
-- (d) a method of a kind determined by the Minister" (no determination deposited; not encoded).
-- s 15D: credit (not the (4A) methods) is allowed for a telephone betting service dealing wholly by voice call whose provider's
-- wagering turnover was or is likely to be under $30 million, with a racecourse presence -- asked as ONE fact.
DECLARE `Way of paying` IS ONE OF
    `a credit card`
    `a wallet or other facility paid from a linked credit card`
    `digital currency`
    `credit from the provider or arranged by it`
    `a debit card or bank transfer`

DECLARE `Payment answer` IS ONE OF
    `Part 2B does not reach it, because it is not a regulated interactive wagering service`
    `Part 2B does not reach it while I am outside Australia`
    `forbidden: the provider must not offer it or accept it from me`
    `allowed`

@export May this wagering service give me credit, or take my bets paid this way (ss 15C, 15D)?
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service` @desc The betting service
      `the way of paying` IS A `Way of paying` @desc How you would pay for your bets
      `I am physically present in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are physically in Australia
      `the provider meets the s 15D small telephone bookmaker conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider is a telephone bookmaker under the $30 million turnover limit with a racecourse presence, dealing with you wholly by voice call (s 15D)
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
DECIDE `May the wagering service take this from me` IS
    IF NOT (`Is it a regulated interactive gambling service` `the service` AND `is a wagering service` `the service`)
    THEN `Part 2B does not reach it, because it is not a regulated interactive wagering service`
    ELSE IF NOT `I am physically present in Australia`
         THEN `Part 2B does not reach it while I am outside Australia`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the way of paying`
              WHEN `a debit card or bank transfer` THEN `allowed`
              WHEN `credit from the provider or arranged by it` THEN
                  IF `is a telephone betting service` `the service` AND `the provider meets the s 15D small telephone bookmaker conditions`
                  THEN `allowed`
                  ELSE `forbidden: the provider must not offer it or accept it from me`
              OTHERWISE `forbidden: the provider must not offer it or accept it from me`

§§ `s 61GB -- what the Register covers`

-- s 61GB: "licensed interactive wagering service means a regulated interactive gambling service that: (a) is a wagering
-- service (see section 4); and (b) has an Australian-customer link (see section 8); and (c) is not provided in contravention
-- of subsection 15AA(3)." Lotteries, games and venue gaming are not wagering services; the Register does not reach them.
@export Is this a licensed interactive wagering service, which the National Self-exclusion Register covers (s 61GB)?
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service` @desc The gambling service
      `I am physically present in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are physically in Australia when you use it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it covered by the Register` IF
        `Is it a regulated interactive gambling service` `the service`
    AND `is a wagering service` `the service`
    AND `I am physically present in Australia`
    AND `the service`'s `the provider holds a State or Territory licence for that kind of service`

§§ `ss 61JA-61JC -- putting myself on the Register`

-- s 61JA(1): "An individual may apply to the Register operator for the individual to be registered". (2): the application
-- must state a number of months, a number of years, or life. (3): months "(a) must be a whole number; and (b) must not be
-- less than 3". (4): years "must be a whole number". (6)(a): it must "include a statement to the effect that the applicant
-- is ordinarily resident in Australia". (7): it may nominate one to five other individuals as nominated support persons
-- "and (b) include a statement to the effect that the applicant has obtained the consent" of each. (9): "An individual is
-- not entitled to make an application ... before the proclaimed start day."
-- s 61JB(1): the Register operator "must attempt to carry out the applicable identification procedure" (set by the Register
-- rules), unless a recognised third-party procedure was done (2) or a previous registration is reactivated (3).
-- s 61JC(1): if the application is made and the procedure was carried out or not required, the operator "must: (c) register
-- the relevant individual ...; and (d) do so within the period ascertained in accordance with the Register rules."
-- No minimum age is in the Act.
DECLARE `Period asked for` IS ONE OF
    `a number of months`
    `a number of years`
    `life`

DECLARE `Application` HAS
    `is made by me, for myself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is made on or after the proclaimed start day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states that I am ordinarily resident in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period asked for` IS A `Period asked for`
    `the number of months or years` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of support persons nominated` IS A NUMBER
    `states that each support person has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my identity has been verified, or need not be` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the period is one the Act allows` IF
    CONSIDER `the application`'s `the period asked for`
    WHEN `a number of months` THEN
            `is a whole number` (`the application`'s `the number of months or years`)
        AND `the application`'s `the number of months or years` AT LEAST 3
    WHEN `a number of years` THEN `is a whole number` (`the application`'s `the number of months or years`)
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the support persons are validly nominated` IF
        `the application`'s `the number of support persons nominated` EQUALS 0
    OR  (    `the application`'s `the number of support persons nominated` AT MOST 5
         AND `the application`'s `states that each support person has consented`)

DECLARE `Registration answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: only I can apply to put myself on the Register`
    `not yet: no one may apply before the proclaimed start day`
    `no: the application must state that I am ordinarily resident in Australia`
    `no: a period in months must be a whole number of at least 3, and a period in years a whole number`
    `no: I may nominate at most 5 support persons, each of whom has consented`
    `not until the Register operator has carried out the identification procedure`
    `yes: the Register operator must register me, within the period set by the Register rules`

@export Can I be registered on the National Self-exclusion Register (BetStop) (ss 61JA-61JC)?
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application` @desc Your application: who makes it, the period asked for, your residence statement, any support persons, and whether your identity has been checked
GIVETH A `Registration answer`
DECIDE `Can I be registered` IS
    IF NOT `the application`'s `is made by me, for myself`
    THEN `no: only I can apply to put myself on the Register`
    ELSE IF NOT `the application`'s `is made on or after the proclaimed start day`
         THEN `not yet: no one may apply before the proclaimed start day`
         ELSE IF NOT `the application`'s `states that I am ordinarily resident in Australia`
              THEN `no: the application must state that I am ordinarily resident in Australia`
              ELSE IF NOT `the period is one the Act allows` `the application`
                   THEN `no: a period in months must be a whole number of at least 3, and a period in years a whole number`
                   ELSE IF NOT `the support persons are validly nominated` `the application`
                        THEN `no: I may nominate at most 5 support persons, each of whom has consented`
                        ELSE IF NOT `the application`'s `my identity has been verified, or need not be`
                             THEN `not until the Register operator has carried out the identification procedure`
                             ELSE `yes: the Register operator must register me, within the period set by the Register rules`

`the most support persons I may have` MEANS 5

@export How many nominated support persons may I have (ss 61JA(7), 61JI(6))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many support persons may I have` IS `the most support persons I may have`

§§ `ss 61JF, 61JG, 61JH -- how long it lasts`

-- s 61JF(1): a registration for a number of months "remains in force for that number of months"; (3) the same for years;
-- (5) for life "remains in force for the life of the individual". (2), (4): subject to ss 61JG, 61JK, 61JM and 61JN; (6) a
-- life registration subject to ss 61JK, 61JM and 61JN -- so it CAN be ended on my own application.
-- s 61JG(5)-(7): on my application the operator "must extend the duration" by the months or years I specify, or to the end
-- of my life.
DECLARE `Registration` HAS
    `the period` IS A `Period asked for`
    `the number of months or years` IS A NUMBER
    `months added by extensions` IS A NUMBER
    `extended to the end of my life` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was registered before this registration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have a nominated support person` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the registration` IS A `Registration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is for life` IF
        `the registration`'s `the period` EQUALS `life`
    OR  `the registration`'s `extended to the end of my life`

GIVEN `the registration` IS A `Registration`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the term in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the registration`'s `the period`
    WHEN `a number of years` THEN 12 TIMES `the registration`'s `the number of months or years` PLUS `the registration`'s `months added by extensions`
    OTHERWISE `the registration`'s `the number of months or years` PLUS `the registration`'s `months added by extensions`

@export Is my registration still in force this many whole months after it came into force (ss 61JF, 61JG)?
GIVEN `the registration` IS A `Registration` @desc Your registration: the period, any extensions, and whether you were registered before
      `months since it came into force` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since your registration came into force
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my registration still in force` IF
       `is for life` `the registration`
    OR `months since it came into force` LESS THAN `the term in months` `the registration`

-- s 61JH(2): if the registration "will expire at a known time, the Register operator must: (a) notify the individual that the
-- individual's registration will expire at that time; and (b) do so at least 14 days before that time." (3): the same notice
-- to each nominated support person. (1): on expiry the operator "must remove the individual's entry".
`the days' warning of expiry` MEANS 14

@export At least how many days before my registration expires must I be told (s 61JH(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days warning of expiry must I get` IS `the days' warning of expiry`

@export Must my support person also be warned before my registration expires (s 61JH(3))?
GIVEN `the registration` IS A `Registration` @desc Your registration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my support person be warned of expiry` IF
        (NOT (`is for life` `the registration`))
    AND `the registration`'s `I have a nominated support person`

§§ `ss 61JK, 61JM, 61JN -- coming off the Register`

-- s 61JK(1): "A registered individual may apply to the Register operator to remove the individual's entry". (2): "However, a
-- registered individual is not entitled to make an application ... during the 3-month period beginning at the time when the
-- individual's registration came into force, unless the individual was previously registered before that time." (3): "(a)
-- be in writing". (4): with "a statutory declaration" that "during the 3-month period ending when the application was made,
-- the registered individual obtained counselling or advice from" a qualified counsellor, a qualified psychologist, a general
-- practitioner or a listed support service "about the registered individual's decision to make the application".
-- (5), (6): unless withdrawn "before the end of the seventh day after the day the application was made", the entry is removed
-- "at the start of the eighth day after the day the application was made"; any nominated support person is told.
DECLARE `Removal application` HAS
    `months since my registration came into force` IS A NUMBER
    `is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a statutory declaration that I had counselling or advice about it in the last 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Removal answer` IS ONE OF
    `not yet: no application in the first 3 months of a first registration`
    `no: the application must be in writing`
    `no: the application needs a statutory declaration that I had counselling or advice about it in the last 3 months`
    `yes: unless I withdraw it by the end of the seventh day, my entry is removed at the start of the eighth day after I apply`

@export Can I apply now to come off the National Self-exclusion Register (s 61JK)?
GIVEN `the registration` IS A `Registration` @desc Your registration, including whether you were registered before
      `the removal application` IS A `Removal application` @desc Your application to come off the Register
GIVETH A `Removal answer`
DECIDE `Can I come off the Register` IS
    IF      `the removal application`'s `months since my registration came into force` LESS THAN 3
        AND (NOT `the registration`'s `I was registered before this registration`)
    THEN `not yet: no application in the first 3 months of a first registration`
    ELSE IF NOT `the removal application`'s `is in writing`
         THEN `no: the application must be in writing`
         ELSE IF NOT `the removal application`'s `has a statutory declaration that I had counselling or advice about it in the last 3 months`
              THEN `no: the application needs a statutory declaration that I had counselling or advice about it in the last 3 months`
              ELSE `yes: unless I withdraw it by the end of the seventh day, my entry is removed at the start of the eighth day after I apply`

@export Has my entry been removed, this many days after I applied to come off (s 61JK(5), (6))?
GIVEN `days since I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole days since the day you applied (that day is day 0)
      `I withdrew the application by the end of the seventh day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you withdrew it in time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my entry been removed` IF
        `days since I applied` AT LEAST 8
    AND (NOT `I withdrew the application by the end of the seventh day`)

@export Must my support person be told that I have applied to come off the Register (s 61JK(5))?
GIVEN `the registration` IS A `Registration` @desc Your registration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my support person be told I applied to come off` IF `the registration`'s `I have a nominated support person`

-- s 61JM: "The Register operator must remove a registered individual's entry ... if the Register operator is aware that: (a)
-- the individual is not ordinarily resident in Australia; or (b) the individual has died." s 61JN(5): "must remove an entry
-- ... if the entry was made in error."
@export Must my entry be removed on grounds other than my own application (ss 61JM, 61JN(5))?
GIVEN `the operator is aware I am not ordinarily resident in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Register operator knows you no longer live in Australia
      `the entry was made in error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your entry was made by mistake
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my entry be removed on other grounds` IF
       `the operator is aware I am not ordinarily resident in Australia`
    OR `the entry was made in error`

§§ `ss 61JD, 61KA, 61LA-61LD -- what the betting companies must then do`

-- s 61KA(3): "A licensed interactive wagering service provider must not provide a licensed interactive wagering service to a
-- registered individual." Offence 500 penalty units (s 61KA(1)); civil penalty 750. Again the provider's, not mine.
DECLARE `Betting answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: it may not be offered to me in Australia at all`
    `no: a licensed wagering service must not be provided to me while I am registered`
    `yes: the Register does not cover it, because it is not a licensed interactive wagering service`
    `yes: it is lawful and I am not registered`
    `the Act does not reach it`

@export May this service take my bets or play while I am on the Register (s 61KA)?
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Gambling service` @desc The gambling service
      `I am physically present in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are physically in Australia
      `I am registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are on the National Self-exclusion Register
GIVETH A `Betting answer`
DECIDE `May this service take my bets` IS
    CONSIDER `Is it lawful to provide this service to me` `the service` `I am physically present in Australia`
    WHEN `prohibited: no one may provide it to me while I am in Australia`
        THEN `no: it may not be offered to me in Australia at all`
    WHEN `unlawful to provide to me: a regulated service whose provider holds no State or Territory licence for it`
        THEN `no: it may not be offered to me in Australia at all`
    WHEN `lawful to provide to me: a regulated service whose provider holds a State or Territory licence for it`
        THEN IF NOT `Is it covered by the Register` `the service` `I am physically present in Australia`
             THEN `yes: the Register does not cover it, because it is not a licensed interactive wagering service`
             ELSE IF `I am registered`
                  THEN `no: a licensed wagering service must not be provided to me while I am registered`
                  ELSE `yes: it is lawful and I am not registered`
    OTHERWISE `the Act does not reach it`

-- s 61LA: no "regulated electronic message to an electronic address" of a registered individual (known, or reckless).
-- s 61LB: no "regulated telemarketing call to a registered individual". s 61LC(2): no "regulated direct marketing material"
-- where it offers or promotes wagering services (s 61GH(1)(d), (e)), or, where it only promotes the provider (61GH(1)(f)),
-- if sent "by a postal service or other like service". s 61LD(2): no disclosure of my name, electronic address, telephone
-- number or address "with the intention that the information be used by the recipient" to market to me, if "(g) the
-- individual has or had a licensed interactive wagering service account with the provider".
DECLARE `Way of marketing` IS ONE OF
    `an email, text or other electronic message`
    `a telemarketing call`
    `physical material offering or promoting wagering services`
    `physical material only promoting the provider, sent by post`
    `physical material only promoting the provider, handed over another way`
    `passing my name or contact details to someone else to market to me`

@export May a licensed betting company market to me this way (ss 61LA-61LD)?
GIVEN `I am registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are on the National Self-exclusion Register
      `the way` IS A `Way of marketing` @desc How the betting company would market to you
      `I have or had an account with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have, or used to have, a betting account with that company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a betting company market to me this way` IF
    -- Part 7B forbids nothing to a provider about an unregistered customer; other laws (the Spam Act 2003, the Do Not Call
    -- Register Act 2006) are not encoded.
    (NOT `I am registered`)
    OR  CONSIDER `the way`
        WHEN `physical material only promoting the provider, handed over another way` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `passing my name or contact details to someone else to market to me` THEN NOT `I have or had an account with it`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 61JD(2): a licensed interactive wagering service provider must not provide, offer or promise "a benefit to an individual
-- ... with the intention of influencing the individual: (e) not to become a registered individual; or (f) to cease to be a
-- registered individual." (4): nor "do an act or thing" with that intention.
@export May a betting company offer me anything to stay off the Register or to come off it (s 61JD)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a betting company offer me something to stay off the Register` IF FALSE

§§ `ss 61MA-61MC -- my betting accounts`

-- s 61MA(2): "A licensed interactive wagering service provider must not open a licensed interactive wagering service account
-- for a registered individual."
-- s 61MB(1)(c), (d): where I had an account and no outstanding or pending bets when I became registered, the provider "must,
-- as soon as practicable after the individual becomes a registered individual: (i) close the account; and (ii) if the
-- account has a credit balance -- pay the individual an amount equal to the credit balance", or, if I owed debts that "could
-- lawfully be recovered by way of deduction from the account", the balance less those debts. s 61MC: if I had outstanding or
-- pending bets, the same "as soon as practicable after the time, or the latest time, when those bets were resolved".
-- s 61MB(1)(f), 61MC(1)(g): "if the account has been closed -- the provider must not reopen, reactivate or reinstate the
-- account". s 61MB(2): this does not prevent opening "a new ... account for the individual if the individual ceases to be a
-- registered individual". s 61MB(9): closure "does not prevent the recovery of a debt".
DECLARE `Betting account` HAS
    `I had outstanding or pending bets when I registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the credit balance` IS A NUMBER
    `debts I owe the provider that may lawfully be deducted from it` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Closing time` IS ONE OF
    `as soon as practicable after I become registered`
    `as soon as practicable after the last of my outstanding bets is resolved`

@export When must the betting company close my account after I register (ss 61MB, 61MC)?
GIVEN `the account` IS A `Betting account` @desc Your betting account as it stood when you registered
GIVETH A `Closing time`
DECIDE `When must my account be closed` IS
    IF `the account`'s `I had outstanding or pending bets when I registered`
    THEN `as soon as practicable after the last of my outstanding bets is resolved`
    ELSE `as soon as practicable after I become registered`

@export How much must the betting company pay me when it closes my account (ss 61MB(1)(c), (d), 61MC(1)(d), (e))?
GIVEN `the account` IS A `Betting account` @desc Your betting account: its balance and any debts you owe the company that may be deducted, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I be paid when my account is closed` IS
    `the larger of` 0 (`the account`'s `the credit balance` MINUS `the account`'s `debts I owe the provider that may lawfully be deducted from it`)

@export May the betting company reopen my closed account, even after I come off the Register (ss 61MB(1)(f), 61MC(1)(g))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my closed account be reopened` IF FALSE

@export May a betting company open a new account for me (ss 61MA, 61MB(2))?
GIVEN `I am registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are on the National Self-exclusion Register
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a new account be opened for me` IF NOT `I am registered`
